---
import Navbar from '../components/Navbar.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import SiteHead from '../components/SiteHead.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');

const lastUpdated = '2026-11-15';

const updatedLabel = new Intl.DateTimeFormat('en-GB', {
  day: 'numeric',
  month: 'long',
  year: 'numeric',
  timeZone: 'UTC',
}).format(new Date(`${lastUpdated}T00:00:00Z`));
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <SiteHead />
    <title>Privacy policy | ECHO</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="How the ECHO university prototype handles browser storage, demo orders, contact forms and third-party services."
    />
  </head>

  <body id="top" class="privacy-page">
    <a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
    <Navbar />

    <main id="main" class="privacy-main">
      <div class="container-fluid echo-container">
        <div class="privacy-document">
          <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="mb-4">
            <ol class="breadcrumb cart-breadcrumb">
              <li class="breadcrumb-item">
                <a href={`${base}/`}>Home</a>
              </li>
              <li class="breadcrumb-item active" aria-current="page">
                Privacy policy
              </li>
            </ol>
          </nav>

          <article
            class="privacy-article"
            aria-labelledby="privacy-heading"
          >
            <header>
              <h1
                id="privacy-heading"
                class="editorial-heading privacy-title"
              >
                privacy policy
                <span class="heading-line" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                <span class="diamond" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              </h1>

              <p class="privacy-updated">
                Last updated: 
                <time datetime={lastUpdated}> {updatedLabel}</time>
              </p>

              <p class="privacy-intro">
                This policy describes the ECHO university prototype,
                its browser-based features and the external services
                used to display its content.
              </p>
            </header>

            <section aria-labelledby="privacy-controller">
              <h2 id="privacy-controller">
                § 1. Personal data controller
              </h2>

              <p>
                ECHO is a fictional audio brand created for an academic
                project. The brand, business details and contact
                information shown on the site are demonstrative.
              </p>

              <p>
                The project author maintains this prototype. Information
                about the project and its demonstration contact details
                is available on the
                <a href={`${base}/contact/`}> Contact page</a>.
                The displayed address and registration information
                do not identify a registered ECHO business.
              </p>
            </section>

            <section aria-labelledby="privacy-purposes">
              <h2 id="privacy-purposes">
                § 2. Purposes and legal bases
              </h2>

              <p>
                The prototype uses information for the following
                demonstration features:
              </p>

              <ul>
                <li>
                  <strong>Contact form: </strong>
                  your name, email, optional phone number, selected
                  department and message are checked in your browser.
                  This form does not send or save your message.
                </li>

                <li>
                  <strong>Cart and demo checkout: </strong>
                  products, quantities, discounts and demo orders are
                  saved in this browser. An order can contain contact
                  details, a delivery address, delivery and payment
                  choices, and company invoice details if entered.
                </li>

                <li>
                    <strong>Newsletter: </strong>
                    the email address is checked in your browser to demonstrate
                    signup. It is not saved or added to a mailing list.
                </li>

                <li>
                  <strong>Demo account: </strong>
                  saved contact details and the default address support
                  the account display and prefill future checkout forms.
                </li>
              </ul>

              <p>
                The contact checkbox demonstrates consent under
                Article 6(1)(a) GDPR. The shopping flow demonstrates
                user-requested steps that, in a real store, may rely on
                Article 6(1)(b). This prototype does not conclude a real
                sales contract or process payments.
              </p>

              <p>
                The ECHO application has no backend that receives these
                form submissions. Hosting, fonts, libraries and embedded
                media can still involve connections to external
                providers, as described below.
              </p>
            </section>

            <section aria-labelledby="privacy-rights">
              <h2 id="privacy-rights">
                § 3. Your rights under GDPR
              </h2>

              <p>
                Where GDPR applies, and subject to the conditions for
                each right, you may request access, correction, erasure,
                restriction of processing or data portability. You may
                also object to processing and withdraw consent where
                consent is the legal basis. Withdrawal does not affect
                the lawfulness of earlier processing.
              </p>

              <p>
                You may lodge a complaint with the competent data
                protection supervisory authority. Questions about this
                academic project should be directed to its author
                through the contact channel supplied with the coursework.
              </p>

              <p>
                For the locally saved demo data, you can edit your
                profile and address on the
                <a href={`${base}/my-account/`}> My account page</a>.
                Your browser's site-data settings let you remove stored
                carts, order history and account details. Clearing that
                data also removes the saved demo history from that browser.
              </p>
            </section>

            <section aria-labelledby="privacy-cookies">
              <h2 id="privacy-cookies">
                § 4. Cookies and browser storage
              </h2>

              <p>
                Cookies and browser storage are different technologies.
                ECHO saves its cart and account information using browser
                storage; the application itself does not set cookies for
                these features.
              </p>

              <div
                class="table-responsive privacy-table-container"
                role="region"
                aria-label="Cookie categories"
                tabindex="0"
              >
                <table class="table privacy-table">
                  <caption>
                    Cookie categories and external services
                  </caption>

                  <thead>
                    <tr>
                      <th scope="col">Category</th>
                      <th scope="col">Use in this prototype</th>
                      <th scope="col">Provider</th>
                      <th scope="col">Duration</th>
                    </tr>
                  </thead>

                  <tbody>
                    <tr>
                      <th scope="row">Essential</th>
                      <td>
                        No first-party cookies are set by the ECHO
                        application itself.
                      </td>
                      <td>ECHO application</td>
                      <td>Not applicable</td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                      <th scope="row">Analytics</th>
                      <td>
                        No first-party analytics cookies are configured.
                      </td>
                      <td>ECHO application</td>
                      <td>Not applicable</td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                      <th scope="row">Advertising</th>
                      <td>
                        No first-party advertising cookies are configured.
                      </td>
                      <td>ECHO application</td>
                      <td>Not applicable</td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                      <th scope="row">Third-party</th>
                      <td>
                        Embedded maps or videos may use cookies or similar
                        technologies, depending on the service and browser
                        settings.
                      </td>
                      <td>Google Maps / YouTube</td>
                      <td>Set by the provider</td>
                    </tr>
                  </tbody>
                </table>
              </div>

              <h3>Data kept in this browser</h3>

              <ul>
                <li>
                  <strong>Cart: </strong>
                  products, quantities and the discount code are stored
                  in localStorage. A sample cart may be created on your
                  first visit.
                </li>

                <li>
                  <strong>Demo orders: </strong>
                  the order history and information entered at checkout
                  are stored in localStorage.
                </li>

                <li>
                  <strong>Account: </strong>
                  saved profile and address details are stored in
                  localStorage.
                </li>

                <li>
                  <strong>Demo session: </strong>
                  the signed-out state is stored in sessionStorage for
                  the current tab session.
                </li>
              </ul>

              <p>
                These localStorage records have no automatic expiry in
                this prototype. They remain until you change or clear
                them, or the browser removes site data. Logging out of
                the demo account preserves the cart, profile and order
                history.
              </p>

              <h3>External services</h3>

              <p>
                The site is hosted on GitHub Pages. Google Fonts supplies
                fonts, and jsDelivr supplies Bootstrap and Bootstrap Icons.
                The contact page embeds Google Maps, and some magazine
                content embeds YouTube. These providers may process
                connection information, such as an IP address, when their
                resources are loaded.
              </p>

              <p>
                You can manage cookies and site storage through your
                browser settings. Blocking external resources may affect
                maps, videos, fonts or other interface elements.
              </p>

              <p>
                Provider information: 
                <a
                  href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement"
                  target="_blank"
                  rel="noopener noreferrer"
                > GitHub privacy statement</a>,
                <a
                  href="https://policies.google.com/privacy"
                  target="_blank"
                  rel="noopener noreferrer"
                > Google privacy policy </a>
                and
                <a
                  href="https://www.jsdelivr.com/terms/privacy-policy-jsdelivr-net"
                  target="_blank"
                  rel="noopener noreferrer"
                > jsDelivr privacy policy</a>.
              </p>
            </section>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </main>

    <Footer />

    <script
      is:inline
      src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap@5.3.3/dist/js/bootstrap.bundle.min.js"
      defer
    ></script>
  </body>
</html>